 "about": [
  "Hanaizumi Shuzo is in the Nango area of Minamiaizu, a district of heavy snow in the mountains of southern Fukushima. It was founded in 1920, took the Hanaizumi name in 1989, and marked its centenary in 2020.",
  "It brews with water from two local springs. One of them, Takashimizu, rises in a forest on the national list of 100 water-source forests. Most of its rice comes from the Aizu region and is polished in the brewery's own mill.",
  "The Roman series, launched in 2007, adds steamed glutinous rice to the mash as a fourth stage."
